sequence:
The AKP should take comfort in its large majority and start to view minority views and even peaceful dissent benignly. This would mean, however, that it is prepared to put in place legislation that is detrimental to its interests and those of the state. It is time for Turkey to start thinking like an opposition, and not an opposition party. The authors would like to express their appreciation to Professor Ramazan Aydın for his valuable comments on the manuscript. Conflict of interest {#d30e1055}
====================

The authors declare that they have no conflict of interest.

With the economic noose poised to tighten around Iran over its suspect nuclear program , the Tehran regime is shaking the foundations of its regime by intensifying its attacks on the Iranian opposition. This is also the regime’s last chance to save itself by appeasing its people and the international community. The regime’s actions include:

1. Refusing to acknowledge the regime’s responsibility for the assassination of Iran’s most prominent opposition leader, Dr. Masoud Rajavi, and his family;

2. Attempting to destroy the website of Rajavi’s main political organization, the National Council of Resistance of Iran (NCRI);

